From: Fabiano Tassotti <fabianotassotti@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] dt-bindings: wifi: ath11k: document OpenWrt extensions

Document the opt-in calibration MAC flag and low-memory datapath profile
used by memory-constrained ath11k boards.

Signed-off-by: Fabiano Tassotti <fabianotassotti@gmail.com>

diff --git a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/net/wireless/qcom,ath11k.yaml b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/net/wireless/qcom,ath11k.yaml
index 0c73329..4b47337 100644
--- a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/net/wireless/qcom,ath11k.yaml
+++ b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/net/wireless/qcom,ath11k.yaml
@@ -49,6 +49,20 @@ properties:
       string to uniquely identify variant of the calibration data in the
       board-2.bin for designs with colliding bus and device specific ids
 
+  qcom,ath11k-calibration-needs-macflag:
+    type: boolean
+    description:
+      Adjust the legacy IPQ5018 calibration MAC flag and checksum after
+      reading the calibration NVMEM cell. Boards without this property use
+      the cell contents unchanged.
+
+  qcom,ath11k-low-memory-datapath:
+    type: boolean
+    description:
+      Use reduced primary RX, monitor buffer, and monitor destination ring
+      sizes to preserve RAM on memory-constrained devices. Boards without
+      this property retain the default datapath ring sizes.
+
   memory-region:
     minItems: 1
     maxItems: 2
